{"text": "On market day, peasants and their wives were walking along every road toward the little town of Goderville. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Bent by years of hard work in the fields, the men moved slowly with long, heavy steps. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The women carried baskets full of chickens and ducks, hurrying to the square where the market was held. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Among them was Maître Hauchecorne of Bréauté, who had just arrived at the edge of the town. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Walking toward the square, he noticed a little piece of string lying on the ground. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Like every true Norman, he believed that anything useful should be picked up, so he bent down slowly. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> His old back hurt from rheumatism, but he took the string from the ground and began to roll it up carefully. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Just then he saw Maître Malandain, the harness maker, watching him from the doorway of his shop. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The two men had once quarreled about a halter, and they had never forgiven each other since that day. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Feeling ashamed to be seen picking up string, Hauchecorne quickly hid it in his pocket and pretended to search the ground.", "alignment": {"characters": ["O", "n", " ", "m", "a", "r", "k", "e", "t", " ", "d", "a", "y", ",", " ", "p", "e", "a", "s", "a", "n", "t", "s", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", "i", "r", " ", "w", "i", "v", "e", "s", " ", "w", "e", "r", "e", " ", "w", "a", "l", "k", "i", "n", "g", " ", "a", "l", "o", "n", "g", " ", "e", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "r", "o", "a", "d", " ", "t", "o", "w", "a", "r", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "l", "i", "t", "t", "l", "e", " ", "t", "o", "w", "n", " ", "o", "f", " ", "G", "o", "d", "e", "r", "v", "i", "l", "l", "e", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "B", "e", "n", "t", " ", "b", "y", " ", "y", "e", "a", "r", "s", " ", "o", "f", " "